## 6. Hard Mods, Mixins, and Patching

Rusty Skylines supports modification systems that may alter or replace portions of the game at build time or runtime, including systems implemented through `rust-mixin`, mixin-style transformations, patch systems, hooks, injections, detours, method replacement, code generation, or comparable mechanisms.

A **“Hard Mod”** means a Mod that modifies Licensed Material through such a mechanism rather than merely using public gameplay APIs or external interfaces.

### 6.1 Commercial Hard Mods

A Hard Mod may be created, distributed, licensed, and commercially sold provided that the Hard Mod itself does not redistribute the Project or a substantial portion of its source code.

A Hard Mod may contain:

* original source code written by the Mod author;
* mixin declarations and patch definitions;
* target selectors, method signatures, hooks, and injection points;
* original replacement or injected implementations;
* configuration and metadata required to apply the Mod;
* small excerpts of Licensed Material reasonably necessary to identify, match, patch, or interface with a target; and
* other material generated specifically to apply the Mod to an authorized copy of Rusty Skylines.

The amount of original code in a Hard Mod is unrestricted. A Hard Mod may contain thousands or millions of lines of code written by its author.

### 6.2 Copied Rusty Skylines Code

A Hard Mod may not intentionally copy and redistribute substantial portions of the existing Rusty Skylines implementation as part of the Mod.

In particular, the following are not permitted in a commercial Hard Mod without separate permission:

* copying substantial Rusty Skylines source files into the Mod;
* reproducing substantial game systems or implementations from the Project;
* copying large sections of existing Rusty Skylines functions merely to avoid writing an original implementation;
* redistributing Rusty Skylines source code as part of a Mod package; or
* presenting copied Rusty Skylines implementation code as original Mod code.

A change from one programming language, file format, namespace, package name, or build system to another does not by itself make copied Licensed Material independent material.

### 6.3 Compiler-Generated Copies

The temporary copying, transformation, compilation, linking, or embedding of Licensed Material that occurs automatically when `rust-mixin` or another compatible tool builds a Hard Mod for use with an authorized copy of Rusty Skylines is permitted.

Such compiler-generated copies do not, by themselves, cause the Mod author's original source code to become Licensed Material.

This permission exists solely to enable the technical operation of the Modding system.

### 6.4 Distribution of Combined Builds

A person may not sell, license, or commercially distribute a complete Rusty Skylines build containing a Hard Mod where the distributed build itself contains substantial portions of Licensed Material, unless separate written permission has been obtained from maxwag9.

A commercial Hard Mod should therefore be distributed as a Mod, patch, mixin, installer, delta, plugin, or other mechanism intended to modify an authorized copy of Rusty Skylines rather than as a separately distributed copy of the entire game.

Nothing in this section prevents a user from locally compiling or applying a Hard Mod to an authorized copy of Rusty Skylines.

### 6.5 No Evasion

A Mod does not become permissible merely because copied Rusty Skylines code is:

* automatically generated;
* reformatted;
* renamed;
* minified;
* obfuscated;
* translated to another language;
* converted into another intermediate representation; or
* distributed only as compiled code.

The relevant question is whether the Mod is redistributing Licensed Material or merely supplying original code and instructions that cause Licensed Material to be modified on the user's authorized copy of the game.

### 6.6 Separate Mod Copyright

Original code written by a Mod author remains the Mod author's own material, subject to this License only to the extent that it incorporates or reproduces Licensed Material.

The Mod author may choose a separate license for original Mod code.

### 6.7 Compatibility

Nothing in this section prevents a Mod from inspecting, targeting, calling, replacing, wrapping, or otherwise interacting with public or observable Rusty Skylines APIs, interfaces, symbols, methods, file formats, protocols, or modding interfaces.

Such interaction alone does not make the Mod Licensed Material.


